GENERATED OUTPUT

The above applies to this tool. It does not apply to the code the tool emits.

Code produced by the generator is yours. You may use, modify, and distribute it
for any purpose, commercially or otherwise, with no obligation to retain a
notice, credit this project, or license your own work in any particular way.
The copyright holder claims no rights in it and asks nothing in return.

This is deliberate: emitted files are meant to be pasted into your repository
and edited as your own, and a notice that had to travel with them would make
that worse for no benefit to anyone. The provenance comment each emitted file
carries names the pattern and the options that produced it so a later reader can
regenerate it; it is a record, not a licence condition, and deleting it costs you
nothing.

Every pattern in this catalogue is an original implementation. Where a pattern's
provenance cites a book, paper, or article, it cites the source of the *idea*;
no third-party code is reproduced, and no third-party licence attaches to
anything the generator emits.
